Dequantize blocks while the frame is still arriving — PUNKTFUNK LOCAL PATCH.

Not upstream. Builds on 0015.

WHY. With the CPU dequant, its 2-3 ms still started only after the last packet of a frame.

WHAT IT DOES. Adds an entry point that dequantizes the blocks of one packet as soon as it lands
(the host already packs whole blocks per packet), so only the GPU passes remain after the last
packet. A lost packet leaves its blocks to the normal full-frame dequant, so loss behaves as
before, and the output is identical to a full-frame decode. Inert unless the caller uses it.
On an LG C5 at 4K60: last packet to decoded 23.2 -> 21.0 ms.

